<title>FRANCE: Arthuis - Eramet minorities compensated.</title>
<headline>Arthuis - Eramet minorities compensated.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Jean Arthuis confirmed on Thursday that minority shareholders in French nickel producer Eramet would be compensated for the expropriation of an Eramet mining licence in New Caledonia.</p>
<p>&quot;These shareholders can be totally assured. There is no question of the state letting them come off badly in any way,&quot; Arthuis told reporters at a press briefing.</p>
<p>He declined to elaborate on compensation of minorities, notably U.S. investment funds.</p>
<p>Eramet confirmed on March 26 that the French government had started a procedure to take away the firm's nickel mining licence for Koniambo in New Caledonia.</p>
</text>
